nd every menu is a listbox that opens from the keyboard and closes with Escape.","An invalid selection is carried by the error ink, a circle icon and the words Not in this Workspace, never by color alone; a locked or disabled control is disabled for assistive technology too.","The session status is a status region, and the popover is reachable from the chip with the keyboard."],"constraints":["Built only from Adapter Widgets (ContextBar, ContextChip, Badge, Button, ListItem, Text, Icon, Kbd, TextInput, Divider, Stack, CanvasStage); no Widget outside the Adapter catalog.","A ContextChip shows its viewport as the preset id and size and its theme as the key, because the Widget has no label lookup; the real controls show the preset and theme labels. The compact summary is a Badge, not a ghost button, because it interpolates the live render context.","A chip with a missing selection is a second chip with the invalid state and the missing key as its literal value, swapped in by the Variant, because a chip cannot change its own value; menus are Stack cards of ListItems placed under their chip.","Every visible string is bound with $i18n except identities (Variant names, Locale tags, viewport and theme names, sizes, key caps and the session and generation identifiers); en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A View is open on the canvas. The bar is the desktop toolbar row; on narrow canvases it drops the dimension words, then collapses into one summary that opens the same four controls stacked.","The base state is the closed bar with the base state, the Workspace default Locale, the first viewport preset and the first theme; the zoom is Fit at 93%. Variants open one menu at a time under the control it belongs to.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset, one Locale and one theme for this View: the bar describes the Workbench chrome of the View page, not the View itself."],"intent":"Show the bar above the canvas where a reviewer chooses the render context of the previewed View (Variant, Locale, viewport and theme), reads the Preview session status and zooms the frame, with the menus each control opens and what the bar does when a selection no longer exists or nothing is authored.","interactionRules":["Each control shows its icon, its label and the value in effect, never a blank placeholder; the four selections are independent, and changing one never changes the Workbench chrome language or appearance.","A dimension with nothing authored says so in its own menu (no Variants, no viewport presets, no themes) and still offers its default; the Variant menu offers a search field once it lists more than eight items.","A selection the Workspace no longer has stays the value of its control in the error ink and is listed in the menu as disabled with the reason, so a link to a removed Variant, Locale, viewport or theme explains itself and changes nothing until another item is chosen.","The Prototype player fixes the Variant of each Flow step, so its Variant control is shown but locked.","The session chip reads Live, Connecting preview, Reconnecting or Preview stopped; its popover gives the one-line state, the Preview session and runtime generation identities, and Retry Preview whenever the session is not live.","The zoom menu offers Fit and 50, 75, 100, 150 and 200 percent and checks the one in effect; zoom out and zoom in stop at the smallest and largest zoom, and every zoom control and the session chip give way while the View has no frame yet."],"references":[{"label":"Phase 5 of the closed loop: dogfood coverage of the core surfaces","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/379#discussioncomment-19257377"}],"requirements":["01a1144e-5174-7ea2-ab72-b5364dd48a03","01a116f0-89b6-7d08-a850-e1ee1aecd51f"]},"variants":{"compact-popover":{"state":{"bar-chips":{"visible":false}